  "solution": {
    "text": "Moles of removed $\\mathrm{CO}_2=\\frac{10^{21}}{6.02 \\times 10^{23}} \\mathrm{~mol}$\n$=1.66 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{~mol}$\nmole of $\\mathrm{CO}_2$ left $=2.8 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{moles}$ total moles of $\\mathrm{CO}_2$ taken initially\n$=(2.8+1.66) \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{~mol}$\nmass of $\\mathrm{CO}_2$ taken initially\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& =4.46 \\times 10^{-3} \\times 44 \\\\\n& =196.24 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{~g} \\\\\n& =196.24 \\mathrm{mg}\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
